# Flow Record Lookup — Field Safety

## Never query LongTextArea fields in a Flow Get Records element

Including a `LongTextArea` field in a Flow's `<queriedFields>` causes a silent UI API wire failure at runtime. The flow element faults with no useful error message.

```xml
<!-- BAD — causes silent runtime fault -->
<recordLookups>
    <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    <queriedFields>Stockout_Summary_JSON__c</queriedFields>  <!-- LongTextArea: never include -->
</recordLookups>

<!-- GOOD — fetch only standard / formula / short-text fields here -->
<recordLookups>
    <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    <queriedFields>Fulfillment_Risk__c</queriedFields>
    <queriedFields>Total_Shortfall_Units__c</queriedFields>
</recordLookups>
```

## Rule of thumb

Exclude any field that is:
- `LongTextArea` or `RichTextArea` type
- Likely to exceed ~32 KB in value

## How to access large text fields in a Flow

Use an Apex Invocable Action with `@AuraEnabled(cacheable=false)` to fetch the field value, then assign the output to a Flow variable. Do not attempt to retrieve it via `Get Records`.

## Diagnosing a flow fault from this cause

1. Open **Setup → Flow → (your flow) → View All Versions → Debug**
2. Look for a fault on a `Get Records` element with message referencing "field is not retrievable" or a generic "An internal error has occurred"
3. Remove large-text fields from `queriedFields` one by one to isolate the culprit
